<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Real first slice of Kinyarwanda/English localization on Android (2026-08-08). See
  bank-mfe/src/i18n's own doc comment for the full context. This app previously had NO
  strings.xml at all in the main :app module: every string was hardcoded directly in
  Kotlin. LoginScreen.kt is itunda's own highest-traffic screen (see its own doc
  comment), so it's the first real screen extracted, matching the same bounded scope
  the web pass used. Uses Android's own real locale-resource mechanism (values-rw/) plus
  AppCompatDelegate.setApplicationLocales for an in-app switcher independent of the
  device's system language, rather than a hand-rolled solution like web's: Android
  already has real, mature tooling for exactly this.
-->
